														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3586896">
									

<p>I'm glad it's provoking questions for you, and this was really about the emotion first and the story second, but there is a story I was trying to tell:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;OK</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The dolls are scientific probes, taking little bits of tissue out of the kids and sending it somewhere (the future). The probes were actually placed by the foundation itself, who sent them back in time to monitor/assassinate these babies. (That's why some of them become inert; those babies just turned out not to be whatever the future foundation is looking for.)</p>
<p>So that's what the researchers discover when they do their special project, and that's why the O5s update the procedures and start letting the machines have the babies instead of keeping them separated. The unanswered question is why they were sent back in the first place, but it must be really important, or we'd never do something so terrible&#8230;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I'm happy to hear I created the atmosphere that I did with the story, and love the idea that maybe it's deep enough for people to have their own interpretations (rather than just too poorly written to understand). Thanks for reading!</p>

							</div>

								
