					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1722371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607460322" alt="Shaggydredlocks" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1722371)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;" >Shaggydredlocks</a></span> <span class="odate time_1504814891 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Sep 2017 20:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3587147">
									

<p>I'd still say that this has some touching up needed, and I'm going to recommend a rewrite.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The SCProcedures could use a bit of work. I'm personally against strike throughs as used here, because it is still clunky to have so much back and forth, and it really takes the impact out of what could be a decent hook.</p>
<p>It could be restructured separately, and simply relabeled &quot;former/current procedures&quot;. I think giving each element (the perceived danger imposed to the -2s vs the mandate to allow -1s to operate) some space to breath would give this line:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3661-1 activation events are not to be interrupted under any circumstance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A <span style="text-decoration: underline;">lot</span> more weight than it currently has, doubly so if it could be more strongly implied that the -2s are infants in the 'former' procedures. A good way to do that would be to change 'humanoid containment cells' to something like 'nursery'.</p>
<p>Couple nitpicks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>contaminated by</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel as though this should be 'containing'? There's no mention of this spreading from one stuffed toy to the next, which this seems to imply.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3661-1A, SCP-3661-1B, and so on.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Once there is a certain number of them, we're going to have to append extra numbers after the letters anyways&#8230;I'd maybe designate the toys 'SCP-3661-A1', A2, A65, etc for ease of reference.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>by making small incisions on the face, neck, or limbs and [REDACTED]2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Based off how this was previously written (being a tech-redaction), is the information relating to their operation/function? As it reads right now, it looks like you're redacting the areas where it makes incisions and I'm not sure that's the intent.</p>
<p>If so, it could be rewritten as &quot;by making small incisions on the face, neck, or limbs and proceeding to [REDACTED]2.&quot;</p>
<p>&#8230;and I just read the new collapsible; it could still stand to be slightly reworded to make it clearer (at this point) that the redaction is covering their action, not their entry point.</p>
<p>Also, having read the hidden content, I can't say the level of redaction is necessary; aside from perhaps the final one revealing it to be Foundation tech.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>That's pretty much it for my nitpicks. Beyond that though, I think the reveal is poorly handled. I can't sustain my disbelief enough. The justification for allowing this is incredibly flimsy, there's simply not enough context to show how they arrived at this conclusion. I don't know what GOI is being referenced (Serpents Hand, I assume, due to the inclusion of the Librarians), or how a temporal paradox factors into the overall picture.</p>
<p>Just because it's Foundation tech doesn't instantly mean there's temporal fuckery afoot - this technology could have been stolen/recreated by spies, for starters. It could have been technology developed concurrently to the SCPF's equipment from another group, or any number of alternate interpretations. The temporal aspect is glossed over instead of cohesively incorporated into the overall narrative, making the entire thing come across as an exercise in shock over substance.</p>
<p>While the recent edits have improved this slightly, it's not at the point where I'd consider reversing my -1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
